\paragraph{Scale (preliminary).}
At 1.7B parameters (Qwen3-1.7B, $\rho{=}0.4$, 2 seeds), adaptive $\bstar$ achieves holdout PPL $13.26 \pm 0.01$ vs.\ uniform $13.27$ ($\Delta{=}{-}0.013$), with OOD results mixed (OWT $\Delta{=}{-}0.009$, Wiki $\Delta{=}{+}0.036$) and downstream accuracy unchanged ($\Delta{=}{-}0.0005$).
The method scales without degradation on holdout and downstream, but the benefit diminishes relative to 0.6B---consistent with larger models being more robust to 0.6B-generated contamination.

